    "type": "/type/text",
    "value": "Science fiction classic about the rise, fall and subsequent rise of a civilization where the peak catastrophe is known as the \"crazy eddy point\". Introduces the concept of frictionless toilets that don't have any water in them but I suspect the authors didn't think it all the way through - I don't recall a negative air pressure that would keep odours in their rightfull place. Nevertheless a fascinating read.\r\nI haven't read this for donkeys years which is why I'm searching for an e-copy."
